    "result_text": "I've implemented both functions in `app/network.py`, and all 8 tests pass (3 existing, 5 I added).\n\n**Timeouts need an extra step.** Setting timeouts on the client isn't enough on its own. HfApi passes `timeout=None` explicitly on most calls (for example `model_info`, `hf_api.py:3172`). In the installed `httpx2`, an explicit `None` means \"no timeout at all\", not \"use the client's setting\" (`httpx2/_client.py:358`). So besides giving the client a 5s connect / 60s read, write and pool timeout, I added a small request hook that applies those timeouts to every request.\n\n**`configure_hub_http(transport=None)`**\n- It registers a client factory with `huggingface_hub.set_client_factory`. That closes any existing shared client, so every `HfApi` instance uses the new one from the next request on.\n- The client sends `X-Acme-Job: nightly-sync` as a default header. huggingface_hub's own headers, including its user agent, are merged in on each request and still go out.\n- It keeps huggingface_hub's own request hook (offline mode, request ID, download counter) and redirect following, and uses `transport` when one is passed.\n- That hook, `hf_request_event_hook`, is imported from the private module `huggingface_hub.utils._http` because it isn't public. That import could break if you upgrade huggingface_hub later.\n\n**`current_revision(repo_id)`**\n- It returns `HfApi().model_info(repo_id, revision=\"main\").sha`.\n- On `httpx2.ConnectError` or `httpx2.TimeoutException` (any connect, read, write or pool timeout), it logs a warning on `app.network` and returns `None`. Everything else still raises, including `RepositoryNotFoundError`.\n- If huggingface_hub is in offline mode (`HF_HUB_OFFLINE`), it raises instead of returning `None`, since that isn't a connection failure or timeout.\n\n**Tests.** I added `tests/test_network.py`, which uses stub transports to check:\n- the header, the user agent and the exact timeouts on requests from two different `HfApi` instances;\n- connection errors and timeou"
  },
